      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Field of five for the Feehan but it'll be exciting with the return of 9yo mare PRIDE OF JENNI (5) who has won this race (at Moonee Valley) the past two years in small fields. She goes very well fresh and a mile is her best trip. She's been jumping out as well as ever and with a few question marks on the challengers, they might just leave her alone again and if they do, she'll lead by as far as she wants and prove very hard to catch. MR BRIGHTSIDE (1) ran 2nd to Jenni in this race two years ago. He was game as ever in the Memsie off a long spell but dropped out last time. Perhaps the ground was a bit firm, this should suit better and he's too tough to write off. ZAMBARDO (4) was ridden negatively fresh but rattled home and can improve. ANOTHER WIL (3) was much better in the Makybe Diva second up albeit had every chance. His best is very good. TREASURETHE MOMENT (6) was okay in the Memsie then awful in the Makybe Diva. Not sure where she's at but we know she's very good if right.",
